# Party banter at Lake Zarovich (the landing and the hill trail). Each node opens with an `if` gate.

~ banter_empty_lake
if visited:lake_zarovich and not flag.bluto_fate
interject tag:curious: A whole lake and not one fish in a year. Where do fish go? Do they have somewhere better?
interject class:druid: Lakes go quiet when something in them is wrong. Or when something on the shore is.
interject tag:blunt: Or the fishers ate them all and blamed the lake. People do that.
endif
-> END

~ banter_bluto_saved
if flag.bluto_fate == "saved"
interject class:cleric: He'd filled his pockets with stones. A man doesn't do that in a hurry. He'd been thinking about it for days.
interject tag:loyal: And then somebody gave him something to row for. That's all it takes, some days. One thing.
endif
-> END

~ banter_bluto_dark
if flag.bluto_fate == "killed" or flag.bluto_fate == "drowned"
interject tag:veteran: The lake got somebody in the end. I keep thinking it was always going to.
interject tag:pious: It was never going to. It just did. There's a difference, and I'll keep insisting on it.
endif
-> END

~ banter_arabelle_lake
if guest:arabelle and visited:lake_zarovich and (tag:cheerful or name:wren_featherfoot)
Arabelle: The lake lady wanted me twice. She doesn't get a third time. I asked.
if tag:cheerful
interject tag:cheerful: Asked who?
else
interject name:wren_featherfoot: Asked who, sprout?
endif
Arabelle: Her. She's not very nice. She was polite about it, though.
endif
-> END
